Package: gganimslide
Type: Package
Title: Reveal 'ggplot2' Layers Step by Step in 'PowerPoint' and 'Beamer' Slides
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Joël Frédéric", "Lattmann", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "jlattmann@student.ethz.ch")
Description: Turns a saved 'ggplot2' object into an animated slide in which
    plot layers, or individual groups such as bars and boxes, appear and
    disappear one after another. ggppt() writes a 'PowerPoint' slide with
    editable vector shapes and native entrance and exit animations; ggtex()
    writes a multi-page PDF plus 'LaTeX' 'beamer' overlay code. All steps are
    cut from one rendered plot, so axes and layers never shift between steps.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/joellattmann/gganimslide, https://joellattmann.github.io/gganimslide/
BugReports: https://github.com/joellattmann/gganimslide/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0),
    grDevices,
    grid,
    stats,
    officer (>= 0.6.2),
    rvg (>= 0.3.0),
    xml2
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
